      "text": [
        " «نَعَمْ» قَالَ فَيُؤَدِّي عَنْهُ مَوْلاَهُ اَلْمُسْلِمُ اَلْجِزْيَةَ قَالَ «نَعَمْ إِنَّمَا هُوَ مَالُهُ يَفْتَدِيهِ إِذَا أُخِذَ يُؤَدِّي عَنْهُ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1679 - Abu Al-Ward asked Abu Ja’far (as) about a Christian slave owned by a Muslim man:\n\"Is jizya required of him?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Yes.\"\nHe then asked: \"Should the Muslim master pay the jizya on his behalf?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"Yes, it is his wealth; he ransoms him by paying on his behalf if he is taken.\""
        ]
      }
